Article 25 (1) The Regional Government facilitates social community institutions as a community self-help effort in the Protection of Women from violence.

2. In order to realize the Protection of Women victims of violence, it is carried out through:
a. providing access to Women victims of violence to obtain education services, health, Social Services and other strategic services;
b. encouraging the involvement of Women victims of violence in the process of resolving problems and recovering victims psychologically and psychosocially as individuals, family members, groups and communities;
c. providing knowledge, skills, character values, morals, and personal resilience, family resilience and Community resilience; and
d. encouraging programs that can increase the independence of Women in the economic, political, legal, social, cultural fields, as well as other strategic fields.

Article 26 Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementing Women's Empowerment and Protection are regulated by Mayor Regulation.
